# MERGE-PARENT-MODEL-SOURCE, a copied method's free input: Box's callable field holds get, so b1, a copy of Box under
# a copy of the unit, holds get's own occurrence there; `b1\get()` runs that occurrence, whose body reads the free
# input a3 through the Wide of its own node.  The call admits the root's a3 to that requirement (2).  HEAD refused the
# read ("a field of a formal admitted by name is not carried by its value").  Exit 7; 81 otherwise.
Wide:
    int: pad 9
    int: x 2
end: Wide
fn: get () int
    return: a3\x
end: get
Box:
    int: v 0
    fn: get
end: Box
b1: merge: Box
a3: merge: Wide
int: r b1\get()
int: ok 7
if: r != 2
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
